# Shell scripts run on Linux (EC2 boot, CI, the SSM deploy). They must keep
# LF line endings even when checked out on Windows — a CRLF shebang breaks
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash`, and Terraform uploads these files verbatim to S3.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Source and config files are linted by Biome, which expects LF. Git already
# stores these as LF (core.autocrlf normalises on commit), but on Windows they
# were being CHECKED OUT as CRLF — so `biome check .` reported a format error on
# essentially every file in the repo, drowning real findings and failing the
# pre-push hook. Pinning eol=lf makes the working tree match what CI lints.
# This changes checkout only; the stored content is unchanged.
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.jsx  text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.cjs  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
